The runner pulls the top unused items from ia_content, generates a brief for each via Claude, stores them in tiktok_briefs, and marks IA items as used.

Exports:
```typescript
export interface BriefRunConfig {
  limit?: number;          // how many items to process (default 20)
  sprint_id: string;
  dry_run?: boolean;       // generate but don't store or mark used
  topic_filter?: string;   // only process items with this topic_id (e.g. 'T01')
  min_score?: number;      // default 40 (briefs only for high-confidence items)
}

export interface BriefRunResult {
  processed: number;
  briefs_generated: number;
  briefs_stored: number;
  errors: string[];
  duration_ms: number;
  briefs: TikTokBrief[];  // all generated briefs (for dry_run inspection)
}

export async function runBriefGenerator(config: BriefRunConfig): Promise<BriefRunResult>;
```

Pipeline:
1. Call getTopUnused(config.limit ?? 20) from ia-scraper storage
2. Filter by config.min_score (default 40) and optional topic_filter
3. For each item: call generateBrief(item, sprint_id)
4. Log: `[brief-runner] [T02] "Apollo 16 Launch" → hook: "The day we touched the moon" (score: 65)`
5. If !dry_run: insertBrief(brief) + markUsed(item.identifier)
6. Return BriefRunResult

Rate limiting: 500ms delay between Claude calls to avoid rate limits.

